### P04 — Valid partially committed plans cannot be conditionally restored

The accepted restore contract verifies and reverses the committed apply prefix under a new guarded lease and finishes restored-held. It contains no activated-only restriction. The candidate instead rejects inventory/staging/verifying/barrier restore at acquireFull with reason `count-restore-requires-complete-apply`. The final validator additionally requires active release fields and a non-null verification stage for all restoring/held plans, preventing safe preactivation rollback even if admission is enabled. This admission restriction predates the last schema patch; it is not solely a validator regression.

Independent probe `/tmp/hudhud-b15-partial-restore-probe.test.mjs` stages one real contribution with unchanged published canonical source, while proving the final baseline is absent and original counter is still 9. It then requires bounded conditional restore to delete that owned created row and finish paused/restored-held without activation. The actual exported API rejects. Exact command:

```sh
/Users/ibrahimqassem/.npm/_npx/52027bd8fc0022aa/node_modules/node/bin/node --test --test-name-pattern='review partial restore probe:' /tmp/hudhud-b15-partial-restore-probe.test.mjs
```

The probe's relative imports are resolved to the frozen `/tmp/hudhud-b15-final-revision` source and existing native fixture. One business assertion executes and fails ERR_ASSERTION/Got unwanted rejection, zero skips; actual domain cause is the activated-only admission refusal, not a missing API, compilation or environment failure. Probe SHA-256 `ed91ad1c99963e5e59f5c9adf62c514ecf9495566797ca293b7bb3a9bbba7f08`; log SHA-256 `96f64f66d45b89b7be3cd7a5791fd80435f01485d5d51c9891d86c2926361eb8`. Durable copies: `B15-partial-restore-review-red.log` and `B15-partial-restore-review-probe.txt`.

Required consolidated correction and evidence:

- Admit conditional restore of genuinely committed inventory/staging/verifying/barrier prefixes without first activating them. Freeze restoreMaxApplyUnit before recovery/inverse receipts; preserve it across bounded calls, fresh lease and lost acknowledgements.
- Permit genuinely absent release proof groups in never-activated restoring/held plans; retain all fields and exact native identity when an actual release exists. Reject mixed/fabricated groups. Retain null verifyStage from pre-verification inventory/staging, or the valid original stage for later interrupted verification/barrier. No new origin flag or wire field is required.
- Every owned inverse still checks fresh canonical source. If no owned counter head exists yet, compare parent.updateTime with original.source.episodeVersion; if a counter head exists, keep its effective native CAS instead of adopting stale original versions or skipping the check. Preserve removal/no-op checks and native receipt conversion.
- Test partial inventory, created-row staging, verification and barrier rollback; maxItems 1 finite progress; lease recovery and inverse lost ACK; same-status parent/comment edits, missing source, ABA/recreate and no resurrection; mixed owned-finalized/partial episode progress where applicable; unchanged/no-op positive controls. Finish held/paused, never release unsafe legacy workers or fabricate activation.

Before partial admission exists, a late-after-admission drift case may fail in setup or be denied earlier; neither is intended source-CAS RED. Record the positive partial rollback business RED honestly, then stage any minimal admission seam and execute permanent late-drift tests before the relevant CAS correction if needed. Parent controls that test/fix sequence. Root source remains early-bootstrap-only; full B15/B16 and findings remain unaccepted. No source, contracts or production operations were changed by this review.


